-- Ghāfir 40:7 sentence 1 — «الَّذِينَ يَحْمِلُونَ الْعَرْشَ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهُ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُونَ لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا» —
-- built in one cycle (km-cyb-ss-build-sentence): the classical tree, every iʿrāb book (four parse; al-Darwīsh, whose 40:7–9 entries begin at
-- 8:13, and the dependency graphs are silent), seven tafsīrs, the derived translation. The prayer that follows is the speech of an
-- omitted «يقولون» — حال from the subject of «يستغفرون» (al-Jadwal, al-Muyassar, al-ʿUkbarī) or explaining it (al-Zamakhsharī, Ibn ʿĀshūr).

